sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2019-boundary-08--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2019-boundary-08: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.52";
    dc:description "Both arms are concrete Xenopus experiments, and the claim's scope is those tadpole systems, which the published measurements cover. The measurements are figures and summaries across several papers, so they can be compiled and cannot be reanalyzed at the animal level. Off-target physiology and single-program replication limit how decisively the existing record separates voltage from other effects of the reagents. The stated species and assay are partly covered; a clean reanalysis is not.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: In genetically normal tadpoles, depolarize the stated cell population and score metastatic-like melanocyte behavior; in oncogene-bearing tadpoles, hyperpolarize by optogenetics or a constitutively open channel and score tumor incidence. Induction by depolarization and prevention by hyperpolarization would confirm the pair of results; either arm failing would refute that half.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Depolarizing drugs and pump constructs have off-target effects.", "Independent replication outside the original laboratory is thin.", "Raw phenotype tables from the cited tadpole papers are not in a repository.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.62"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.516"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2019-boundary-08--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2019-boundary-08 by Grok 4.7: 0.35";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.35"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2019-boundary-08--grok>.
